\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Tamil (ISO 639-3 tam; Glottocode tami1289) is a Dravidian language and an official language in parts of India, used as a language of instruction. The language is very well resourced. This report is a short starting list from limited searching, not a complete survey.
\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Tamil Nadu School Education Department e-books page (Classes 1--12, Tamil medium available), reported by guides as \url{https://tnschools.gov.in/scert}; I did not see this page itself in search results, only guides citing it. Third-party mirror sites also appeared and are not recommended.
\item Samacheer Kalvi textbook background: \url{https://patrimoine.minesparis.psl.eu/Wiki/index.php/Samacheer_Kalvi_Wikipedia}
\end{itemize}
\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item University of Madras Tamil Lexicon (1924--1936), online at DSAL: \url{https://dsal.uchicago.edu/dictionaries/tamil-lex}
\item Tamil Lexicon, Wikipedia: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamil_Lexicon_dictionary}
\item Tamil Lexicon Vol. 1 part 1 (PDF, Tamil Digital Library): \url{https://tamildigitallibrary.in/assets/docs/uploads/primary_files/book/TVA_BOK_0025899/TVA_BOK_0025899_Tamil_lexicon_Vol_1_part_1.pdf}
\item Lexicographic Practice in Tamil (Tamil Digital Library): \url{https://www.tamildigitallibrary.in/admin/assets/book/TVA_BOK_0006332_Lexicographic_Practice_in_Tamil.pdf}
\item Lexilogos Tamil dictionary links: \url{https://lexilogos.com/english/tamil_dictionary.htm}
\item Learn Tamil links (ibiblio): \url{https://www.ibiblio.org/learntamil/links.htm}
\end{itemize}
\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None specifically sought or found.
\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Tamil Virtual Academy (digital library and distance education, Government of Tamil Nadu): \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamil_Virtual_Academy}
\item Tamil Wiktionary entry (sample): \url{https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E0%AE%A4%E0%AE%AE%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B4%E0%AE%9A%E0%AF%8D%E0%AE%9A%E0%AE%BF}
\end{itemize}
\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Tamil is already a language of instruction in Tamil Nadu, with a state curriculum. Further searching is needed for the official curriculum frameworks, Sri Lankan and Singaporean Tamil curricula, and audio and video resources.
\end{document}
